 "build_recommendation": "Replace hand-written instinct content with a shipped pack of cross-repo priors: per (learned intent, head) first-attempt sufficient statistics (s, n, kappa, intent rate) fitted offline over the corpus; bind candidates by path existence in the checkout (adage-instincts::bind); posterior = prior + the repo's own first attempts with a 10%-quantile gate (score.rs Beta backoff with a cross-repo parent and fitted kappa); deliver as a predictive PreToolUse rewrite when the running head's posterior < 0.5. Expected value: parity with U11 predictive on Python/.venv repos (+1.45 to +1.6 calls, ~3-3.4% of $ per task, CI 2.2-4.4%) with no hand rule; the upside is coverage of new friction families as the corpus grows, not extra savings per task.",
